{
  "id": "UP040",
  "version": "2.0",
  "title": "Hydrocelectomy",
  "description": "A hydrocelectomy removes fluid collecting around your testicle due to hydrocele. This brief outpatient procedure takes 30-45 minutes where your urologist makes a small incision to access and drain the fluid, then closes the membrane lining to prevent recurrence. Local anesthesia provides comfort. Afterwards, you'll have mild groin soreness and swelling for 1-2 weeks. You should avoid heavy lifting and strenuous activity for 2-3 weeks. Most people return to work within a week. The procedure is very successful with low recurrence rates. Your scrotal swelling and discomfort resolve completely.",
